{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The smaller caliper felt useful because measuring hose diameters and fittings would help me choose parts for the kinds of repairs reflected in my clamp purchases.",
    "The assorted heat shrink tubing complements my crimp terminals, while the epoxy offers a way to handle rigid repairs where my tape and vinyl cement may not work."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The large, single-size heat shrink tubing has no clear use for me right now; the assorted kit gives me sizes I could match to different wire connections.",
    "Ten tubes of glue and a thousand small gloves exceed my current needs, and I cannot confirm the glove fit. The larger caliper is relevant, but I would choose the smaller one this time.",
    "Locking nuts, marking flags, and a temperature gun require specific tasks I have not indicated; owning repair supplies and an inspection camera does not make those tasks current needs."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My repair purchases seem to have been treated as interest in almost any workshop supply, even when I cannot connect it to a job.",
    "My past bulk tape purchase seems to have been taken as a broader preference for large quantities, although my needs differ by supply."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "Compatibility matters: tubing sizes should suit my wire connections, and measuring tools should help with the hoses and fittings I work with.",
    "I care about whether an item adds a useful repair capability in an appropriate size and quantity, rather than simply resembling something I bought before."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations understood my practical repair interests but sometimes stretched them into supplies, quantities, and specialized tasks I do not currently need."
}"}
